DTSTAMP:20261029T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261104T190000
SUMMARY:The Edmund Fitzgerald: the physics of a storm
LOCATION:UWF Tech Campus Library\, 1170 Martin Luther King Jr Blvd\, Fort W
 alton Beach\, FL 32547
DESCRIPTION:Wednesday 11/4 · 6:00 PM\n\nUWF librarian Travis Souther expla
 ins the physics behind the 1975 loss of the Edmund Fitzgerald\, the larges
 t freighter on the Great Lakes\, in a storm on Lake Superior. The talk is 
 part of the library's Forces of Nature\, Failures of Man series. It takes 
 place in the Student Government Association room.\n\nPrice: Free\n\nDetail
 s: https://coastaleventures.com/events/ev-uwf-edmund-fitzgerald-talk-1104.
 html
URL:https://coastaleventures.com/events/ev-uwf-edmund-fitzgerald-talk-1104.
 html
CATEGORIES:STEM and learning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
